│ patch_description        │ The score of 0.00 strongly suggests the produced configurations are being judged invalid  │
│                          │ (points outside the container). The root cause is the incorrect barycentric conversion in │
│                          │ `_clip_bary`: the formula for the weight of vertex (0,0) is wrong, so clipped points can  │
│                          │ land outside the triangle, and the local search then wanders in an infeasible region      │
│                          │ producing invalid output. Fixing the clip guarantees every candidate point stays strictly │
│                          │ inside/on the triangle, so the optimizer operates on valid configurations. Second, the    │
│                          │ warm start is improved by a symmetric construction (points mirrored about the vertical    │
│                          │ median x=0.5) which is known from Heilbronn-triangle practice to be near-optimal for      │
│                          │ small n, and the local search is made more effective by testing both symmetric and        │
│                          │ single-point moves with a slightly larger budget. Both changes preserve determinism       │
│                          │ (fixed seed) and the fallback path.                                                       │
