│ patch_description        │ The original function returned all points at (0,0), yielding a min triangle area of 0. I  │
│                          │ replace it with a deterministic multi-start local optimization. Points are described by   │
│                          │ 22 free coordinates constrained (via linear inequalities) to lie inside the equilateral   │
│                          │ triangle. The objective maximizes the smallest triangle area among all C(11,3)=165        │
│                          │ triplets. Since min() is non-smooth, I use a log-sum-exp "soft-min" with progressively    │
│                          │ increasing sharpness (p = 10, 30, 100) over three SLSQP stages, which produces a smooth   │
│                          │ gradient that concentrates on the smallest triangles. Several deterministic starts are    │
│                          │ used (a triangular lattice selection, boundary-biased layouts, and seeded perturbations); │
│                          │ the best true (hard) minimum-area configuration is returned. The result comfortably       │
│                          │ exceeds the benchmark min_area_normalized of ~0.0365, and runtime is kept bounded by      │
│                          │ fixed iteration limits. A safe fallback returns the best valid configuration if any       │
│                          │ optimization stage fails.                                                                 │
