│ patch_name               │ vectorized_jac_and_relocation                                                             │
│ patch_description        │ Two targeted improvements: (1) The current Jacobian contains a Python loop over all       │
│                          │ C(11,3)=165 triples, called on every SLSQP iteration — this is the dominant cost and      │
│                          │ makes the optimizer painfully slow. The gradient can be fully vectorized with             │
│                          │ `np.add.at`, giving identical results but ~100x faster per call, allowing more            │
│                          │ starts/iterations within the same time budget. (2) Per the recommendation, add a hybrid   │
│                          │ global relocation phase after the SLSQP runs: when local refinement stalls, pick the      │
│                          │ point in the worst triplet and teleport it to a fresh sqrt-transformed barycentric        │
│                          │ sample, accepting if min_area improves, followed by small Gaussian polish. This escapes   │
│                          │ local optima where pure gradient descent on a smooth softmin gets stuck.                  │
