│ patch_description        │ The prior proven pattern (smooth-softmin multi-start local optimization) reached 0.76 of  │
│                          │ benchmark in ~16s for only 4 starts. The single lowest-risk improvement is best-of-N over │
│                          │ many more restarts wrapped in an anytime time budget: keep the softmin objective but      │
│                          │ anneal temperatures with fewer Powell iterations per pass (Powell's cost is dominated by  │
│                          │ line searches, so trimming maxiter lets many more starts fit), generate more              │
│                          │ deterministic starts (perturbations of the symmetric base plus seeded random ones), and   │
│                          │ loop `while time.time() - t0 < 25`, always keeping the best configuration found. Since    │
│                          │ the min-area objective is highly multimodal, best-of-N over independent starts is the     │
│                          │ most reliable way to push combined_score above 1.0. Determinism is preserved via a fixed  │
│                          │ seed; feasibility is guaranteed by the softmax barycentric parametrization; a hardcoded   │
│                          │ fallback remains if optimization fails.                                                   │
