│ patch_name               │ hybrid_slsqp_plus_hillclimb                                                               │
│ patch_description        │ This crossover combines the best elements of both parents: (1) the gradient-based SLSQP   │
│                          │ smooth-minimum optimizer from the inspiration program (which is effective but slow due to │
│                          │ a Python-loop Jacobian), and (2) the fast vectorized min-area evaluation and stochastic   │
│                          │ hill-climbing refinement from the current program. Key improvements: the Jacobian is      │
│                          │ fully vectorized with `np.add.at` (removing the 165-triplet Python loop), fewer starts    │
│                          │ are used with an iteration budget to keep runtime reasonable, a deterministic stochastic  │
│                          │ polish phase (single- and two-point moves with clipping) refines the SLSQP output to      │
│                          │ escape soft-min bias, and the fallback path now uses a verified distinct-point lattice so │
│                          │ the result never degenerates to zero area even if optimization fails. Feasibility is      │
│                          │ guaranteed by final projection into the triangle.                                         │
