│ patch_description        │ Two changes: (1) The current `_optimize` gradient uses a Python loop over all 165 triples │
│                          │ inside every SLSQP jacobian call, which caused the huge 3.23s eval time while yielding    │
│                          │ only 0.03 score (and the polish phase was dropped, explaining the collapse from 0.46).    │
│                          │ Replace the loop with a fully vectorized `np.add.at` scatter-add gradient —               │
│                          │ mathematically identical but orders of magnitude faster, freeing time budget. (2)         │
│                          │ Re-introduce the batched worst-triplet guided random polish (the component that produced  │
│                          │ the 0.46 result in only 0.39s), applied after projecting the SLSQP solution into the      │
│                          │ triangle. The polish moves points belonging to the currently-worst triplets, evaluates a  │
│                          │ whole batch of candidate moves at once via vectorized min-area computation, and includes  │
│                          │ occasional global teleport escapes. This combination of fast SLSQP refinement plus guided │
│                          │ stochastic polish is the best-performing architecture among the prior programs.           │
