│ patch_name               │ targeted_gradient_annealing                                                               │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the slow softmax-Powell multi-start with a fast, deterministic direct-coordinate  │
│                          │ local search using gradient-informed moves: identify the worst triangle and move its      │
│                          │ three vertices perpendicular to their opposite sides (the exact gradient directions of    │
│                          │ that triangle's area), projecting back onto the triangle for feasibility. A shrinking     │
│                          │ step anneals the search, and randomized escape moves on the worst triplet avoid local     │
│                          │ stalls. This is far cheaper per iteration than the smooth-softmin Powell approach (which  │
│                          │ pays softmax+exp+log over 165 triples per function call), so many restarts fit well under │
│                          │ the previous 15.8s runtime while improving the achievable min area.                       │
