│ patch_description        │ Crossover of the random-restart local search (program 3) with the symmetric ring-seed     │
│                          │ layout (program 1). Key improvements: (1) warm-start the search with the structured ring  │
│                          │ layout (center + two staggered 5-point rings) in addition to uniform random barycentric   │
│                          │ starts, which lands the optimizer directly in a good basin; (2) keep the fully-vectorized │
│                          │ batched candidate evaluation (_min_area_batch) so each iteration tests K perturbations at │
│                          │ once; (3) keep the fast barycentric projection for feasibility; (4) focus perturbations   │
│                          │ on points from the few worst triplets while allowing occasional all-point moves to escape │
│                          │ local optima; (5) an annealed step schedule with geometric decay. Deterministic via fixed │
│                          │ seeds, with a safe fallback returning the projected ring layout on any failure.           │
