│ patch_description        │ This rewrite keeps the feasibility-by-construction idea (barycentric parametrization)     │
│                          │ from the softmax program but replaces the slow, ill-conditioned Powell-in-logits approach │
│                          │ with a fundamentally better-conditioned scheme: (1) parametrize directly in barycentric   │
│                          │ weights with a clean simplex-projection (clipping + renormalization) instead of softmax   │
│                          │ logits, which distorts gradients near the boundary; (2) optimize a top-k "active-set"     │
│                          │ soft-min — only the k smallest triangles drive the objective — which concentrates the     │
│                          │ optimizer's effort on the binding constraints instead of averaging over all 165 triples;  │
│                          │ (3) use L-BFGS-B with annealed temperatures, which is far more efficient in 33 dims than  │
│                          │ Powell was in 33 dims of logits; (4) multi-start with deterministic perturbations around  │
│                          │ a hand-designed symmetric seed plus reflected-pair starts. A strictly-positive min-area   │
│                          │ guard with a rescue restart prevents the silent-degenerate failure mode observed in       │
│                          │ earlier generations.                                                                      │
