                        Patch Metadata - Gen 34/200 - Novelty: 1/3 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/3                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ batched_best_of_k_search                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ The current program is slow (7.12s) because it evaluates candidate perturbations one at a │
│                          │ time with a Python-level triple loop. The prior faster programs show that vectorizing     │
│                          │ candidate evaluation is the key to both speed and quality: with a batched best-of-K move  │
│                          │ we can afford many more restarts and a finer multi-scale step schedule within the same    │
│                          │ wall time, which directly improves min_area (the primary objective). Additionally,        │
│                          │ focusing moves on the points of the K worst triplets (rather than only the single worst)  │
│                          │ helps escape poor basins. I therefore: (1) add `_areas_all` and a `_min_area_batch`       │
│                          │ helper, (2) replace the scalar inner loop with a vectorized best-of-24 perturbation over  │
│                          │ the movers of the 6 worst triplets plus a fallback global sweep, and (3) increase         │
│                          │ restarts to 25 with early bail-out on hopeless starts so time budget is spent on good     │
│                          │ basins.                                                                                   │
│ num_applied              │ 2                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0109                                                                                   │
│ error_attempt            │ None                                                                                      │
│ system_prompt_id         │ None                                                                                      │
