│ patch_name               │ barycentric_pipeline                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ Restructure the solver into a clean pipeline over barycentric coordinates (guaranteeing   │
│                          │ feasibility by construction instead of post-hoc projection): (1) diverse deterministic +  │
│                          │ seeded starts, (2) staged softmin SLSQP with vectorized analytic gradients, (3) targeted  │
│                          │ worst-triplet refinement — a discrete polish that moves only points of the argmin         │
│                          │ triplet, with perpendicular escape directions away from the constraining line, batched    │
│                          │ and vectorized, (4) global teleport restarts from the hot set. Barycentric                │
│                          │ parameterization removes constraint handling from the optimizer (only box bounds remain)  │
│                          │ and makes every intermediate point feasible, so the polish accepts candidates that the    │
│                          │ old clipped-xy version rejected. The worst-triplet polish directly attacks the primary    │
│                          │ objective (the exact discrete min), which softmin only approximates.                      │
