│ patch_name               │ mirror_symmetric_starts                                                                   │
│ patch_description        │ The known near-optimal Heilbronn configurations for n=11 in an equilateral triangle       │
│                          │ exhibit strong reflection symmetry about the vertical median (x = 0.5). Random starts     │
│                          │ almost never have this structure, so SLSQP and polish must fight an asymmetric basin.     │
│                          │ Adding deterministic mirror-symmetric starts — one centroid point plus 5 mirrored pairs — │
│                          │ dramatically broadens coverage of high-quality basins at negligible cost (they are cheap  │
│                          │ to construct and deterministic). Each pair is a point plus its reflection (x, y) -> (1-x, │
│                          │ y), guaranteeing the reflection symmetry that optimal layouts exploit. This directly      │
│                          │ implements the recommendation to diversify mirror-symmetric starts. The clip projection   │
│                          │ preserves symmetry since the triangle is symmetric about x=0.5, so these starts stay      │
│                          │ feasible after projection. This should raise min_area_normalized, and combined_score,     │
│                          │ without materially increasing eval_time (SLSQP converges quickly from symmetric starts    │
│                          │ since gradients w.r.t. mirrored coordinates cancel).                                      │
