│                          │ move each of its three points along the unit perpendicular direction away from the        │
│                          │ opposite side — the exact direction gradient of the triangle's area — with a shrinking    │
│                          │ step size. This "worst-triangle expansion" polish is the classical refinement for         │
│                          │ Heilbronn-style max-min problems and squeezes out extra area after the stochastic search  │
│                          │ stalls, since increasing the smallest triangle's area only ever requires moving its own   │
│                          │ three points.                                                                             │
