                        Patch Metadata - Gen 42/200 - Novelty: 1/3 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/3                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ k_worst_multistart_polish                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ The current local search only perturbs the 3 points of the single worst triplet, which    │
│                          │ easily cycles: many near-degenerate triples compete, and the search oscillates between    │
│                          │ them without structural escape. Two targeted improvements:                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **k-worst point set**: instead of only the worst triplet's points, gather the union of │
│                          │ points appearing in the k=5 smallest-area triples. This spreads the gradient/mutation     │
│                          │ signal across all binding constraints (as recommended), avoiding the dilution and cycling │
│                          │ of a single binding constraint.                                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. **Longer budget with more candidates**: the run finishes in 5.3s while the prior 20s   │
│                          │ run also scored only 0.71 — the incremental area updates make each step cheap, so we can  │
│                          │ afford more restarts, more candidates (K=48), and a full polish phase. Raising the budget │
│                          │ to 17s trades a small eval_time cost for a much better chance to find the high-area       │
│                          │ boundary configurations known for n=11 (best arrangements place most points on the        │
│                          │ boundary).                                                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Both changes are consistent with the existing incremental machinery (`best_of_k_move`     │
│                          │ already supports any point index).                                                        │
│ num_applied              │ 3                                                                                         │
