│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ topk_softmin_objective                                                                    │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the uniform 165-triple softmin with a top-k (k=20) softmin in both the objective  │
│                          │ and its Jacobian. Currently the softmax weights w spread gradient mass over all 165       │
│                          │ triplets, most of which are far from binding — this dilutes the optimization signal and   │
│                          │ biases SLSQP toward configurations where merely "average" triangles are comfortable       │
│                          │ rather than pushing up the binding worst-case ones. By taking the 20 smallest areas and   │
│                          │ applying the temperature-annealed log-sum-exp over only those, the gradient concentrates  │
│                          │ on the constraints that actually determine the objective, which is the smooth analogue of │
│                          │ the discrete worst-triplet targeting that produced the biggest historical gains. The `m = │
│                          │ ar.min()` shift is retained for numerical safety. Changes are confined to `obj` and `jac` │
│                          │ inside `_optimize`; the rest of the pipeline (starts, polish, hybrid loop) is untouched.  │
