│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ worst_triplet_refine_between_temps                                                        │
│ patch_description        │ Following the recommendation, I interleave discrete worst-triplet refinement between the  │
│                          │ Powell annealing stages inside `_softmin_refine`. After each temperature stage, the       │
│                          │ argmin triplet is identified via a vectorized cross-product scan, and a cheap Powell pass │
│                          │ optimizes only that triplet's 9 logits against a small softmin objective. This focuses    │
│                          │ effort exactly on the binding constraint (the triplet that actually determines the score) │
│                          │ while the global softmax keeps all points inside the triangle. Since only 9 variables are │
│                          │ perturbed and the objective only evaluates ~few triples plus the runner-up check, each    │
│                          │ refine costs far less than a global stage but can directly raise the minimum area,        │
│                          │ breaking the 0.03 plateau. The refined result is accepted only if the true global min     │
│                          │ area improves, so it can never hurt.                                                      │
